15. Pricing & Profitability Analytics

Revenue alone does not tell management whether a product is financially attractive.

A Data Analyst can calculate:

Revenue – Discounts – Product Cost – Distribution Cost = Contribution

The analysis can be performed at:

- Product level
- Territory level
- Distributor level
- Division level
- Customer level

Key questions

- Which products have the highest margins?
- Which products generate high revenue but low margins?
- How do discounts affect profitability?
- Which regions provide better contribution?
- Which promotional campaigns generate profitable sales?

Business impact

Better profitability analysis allows management to optimize pricing and promotional decisions.

